        "fgco2": {
          "type": "data",
          "description": "sea-air CO2 fluxes for the global ocean calculated with kw * sol * dfco2 * (1 - ice). Positive = upward flux. dfco2 is from OceanCarbNN. kw = 0.271 * U^2 * (660 / Sc)^0.5 (U^2 = ERA^2 at native resolution); sol = solubility of CO2 in seawater using ESA-CCI temperature (or NOAA OISSTv2), and stacked salinity. ice fraction is from the SST product. More information about these variables can be found in their respective metadata.",
